# Dark UI: Light text on dark background (Hermes)

Hermes terminals and WPF panels use a dark theme.

## Hard rule

**Light text on dark background** for **every** visual state:

- default, hover, focus, pressed, selected, disabled
- **ToolTip** popups
- ComboBox / dropdown popups
- buttons that override `Style` for Visibility / layout only

Never light/white backgrounds under light (or pale gray) text — including stock WPF Button/ToolTip chrome.

## WPF specifics

- Global styles live in `Hermes.Wpf/Resources/Styles.xaml` (`Button`, `ToolTip`).
- If a control needs an extra `Style` (e.g. hide unless ProjectManager): **always** `BasedOn="{StaticResource {x:Type Button}}"` so dark hover template is kept.
- Hover = **darker** shade of the same family (`#2B79EF`, `#383f49`, darker red/green) — text stays `#FFFFFF` / `#EAECEF`.
- ToolTip: background `#2B3139`, text `#EAECEF`, border `#383f49` — never system white tooltip.

```xml
<!-- ✅ GOOD: keep dark Button chrome -->
<Style TargetType="Button" BasedOn="{StaticResource {x:Type Button}}">
  <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed"/>
</Style>

<!-- ❌ BAD: replaces template → stock light hover, invisible white text -->
<Style TargetType="Button">
  <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed"/>
</Style>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: dark hover, light text -->
<Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
  <Setter TargetName="Bd" Property="Background" Value="#383f49"/>
  <Setter TargetName="Cp" Property="TextElement.Foreground" Value="#FFFFFF"/>
</Trigger>
```

## Palette

| Role | Color |
|------|-------|
| Background | `#0B0E11`, `#181A20`, `#2B3139` |
| Hover | `#383f49`, `#252C3B`, `#2B79EF` (or darker brand) |
| Text | `#EAECEF`, `#FFFFFF` |
| Muted | `#848E9C` |
| Accent | `#F0B90B` → `#F8D12F` |
| ToolTip | bg `#2B3139`, text `#EAECEF` |
